			"Message": "build(Cocoon): Refactor ESBuild configuration and regenerate artifacts\n\nDecompose the monolithic ESBuild configuration in `Source/ESBuild.js` into a modular structure under `Configuration/ESBuild/`. Separate concerns by extracting base, target, and compile configs into distinct modules, and isolate environment constants. This improves maintainability and aligns the build pipeline with the project's PascalCase conventions.\n\nAdditionally, introduce `Configuration/Mountain/Config.js` to define and validate gRPC connection parameters for the Mountain backend, ensuring robust IPC setup with environment variable overrides. Regenerate all `Target/` build artifacts, TypeScript definitions, and the `RouteManifest` to reflect these structural changes and the ongoing modularization of VS Code API namespaces.\n\nThe extension host build pipeline now utilizes a cleaner, factorized configuration while preserving all previous functionality and external dependency exclusions.",
			"SHA": "245048602b164993f64c2297ce68e249b99e2479"
		},
